course: dictionary
lesson: 10971
title: Meaning and feeling: want
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Want means to wish to have or do something. «I want a new bike» means you would like one, even if you do not really need it. The words around the word tell you what kind of wish it is.
explain: Look for the word after it. «Want to» followed by a verb, as in «I want to play», means you would like to do that thing. «Do you want more?» asks if you would like some more. Context clues help you see which meaning fits.
explain: The same word can mean something else. On a poster, «wanted» means the police are looking for someone. Always check the sentence around the word before you decide what it means.
explain: Wants and needs are not the same. Food is a need, because you must have it to live. A toy is a want, because you would like it but can live without it. In maths, the difference between what you have and what you want shows how many more you need.
fact: Want means to wish to have or do something.
fact: «Want to» followed by a verb means you would like to do it, as in «I want to play».
fact: «Wanted» on a poster means the police are looking for someone.
fact: Wants are things people wish for but do not really need. Food is a need; a toy is a want.
fact: «A boy in Arizona wants a bearded dragon for his birthday» shows a want as a wish for something special.
exercise: «A boy in Arizona wants a bearded dragon for his birthday.» What does wants mean here? | Is looking for | Must have to stay alive | Is afraid of | *Wishes to have
exercise: On a poster, «WANTED» means what? | *The police are looking for someone | Someone is very hungry | Someone has a present to give | The poster is for sale
exercise: Which of these is a want, not a need? | *A new toy | Water | Food | Sleep
test: What does «want to» mean in «I want to play»? | Is afraid to play | Has already finished playing | Must play every day | *Would like to play
test: In the Golden Rule, «do to others what you would want them to do to you», what does want mean? | Dislike | Forget | *Wish for | Need to
exam: «A computer does not feel, want or know anything» means a computer | *Has no wishes of its own | Wants to help people all day | Knows everything that people know | Feels happy when it works well
